> where is 1/x defined for u8 x?
  ucas: it(x: u8) = 1/x
  ucas: domain it
domain of it:
  x: u8, 0..255
  requires x != 0  (in 1/x)
  defined at 255 of 256 points
  defined for: 1..255
  undefined e.g. at x=0
  C undefined behaviour at 1 points, e.g. x=0
  over all 256 points of the domain
> give me a table of x^2 for x from 0 to 5
  ucas: it(x in 0..5) = x^2
  ucas: table it
  x=0  ->  0
  x=1  ->  1
  x=2  ->  4
  x=3  ->  9
  x=4  ->  16
  x=5  ->  25
